> The scroll of enchantment replaces the enchant weapon and enchant armor
> scrolls, and reading it allows you to attempt to enchant any item in
> your inventory.
> 
> * A scroll of enchantment has a base price of 80 zorkmids, and requires
> 16 magic marker charges to write.
> * You now increase the enchantment of stat-increasing rings (increase
> damage etc.) through enchantment scrolls, instead of charging scrolls.
> * Enchanting certain potions (like fruit juice) can change them into
> other potions (like see invisible).
> * Enchanting non-magical musical instruments changes them into their
> magical counterparts.
> * A confused reading of the scroll allows you to attempt to erodeproof
> any item in your inventory.
> * You can choose to fireproof scrolls and spellbooks. Fireproofed
> scrolls and spellbooks cannot be burned by fire or blanked by water.
> 
> The patch also has the following auxiliary effects:
> 
> * Made it so that enchanting an item doesn't alter its b/u/c status.
> * Altered the feedback messages for Magicbane enchantment, as I believe
